---
/**
 * Deliberately *not* an auto-redirect. Every real old URL has its own redirect
 * page, so anything reaching this one is a path that never existed — and
 * Google's guidance is not to funnel unknown 404s to a homepage, which reads
 * as a soft 404. A notice with a link is the honest version.
 *
 * Note this is also the 404 for the project sites sharing errorsignal.dev
 * (/coppermind/ and friends), which is another reason it must not redirect.
 */
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>404 — not found</title>
    <style>
      html {
        color-scheme: dark;
      }
      body {
        margin: 0;
        min-height: 100vh;
        display: grid;
        place-content: center;
        gap: 0.75rem;
        padding: 2rem;
        background: #0b0d12;
        color: #c8cfdc;
        font: 400 14px/1.6 ui-monospace, 'JetBrains Mono', Menlo, monospace;
        text-align: center;
      }
      h1 {
        margin: 0;
        font-size: 2rem;
        color: #ff6b81;
      }
      p {
        margin: 0;
      }
      a {
        color: #7fd4ff;
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <h1>404</h1>
    <p>This page does not exist.</p>
    <p>errorsignal.dev has moved to <a href="https://memerson.com/">memerson.com</a>.</p>
  </body>
</html>
